    a: "20% of 150 is 30. You multiply 150 by 0.20 to get the answer. You can use the What is X percent of Y mode in this calculator to confirm any similar problem instantly."
  - q: "How do I calculate percentage change?"
    a: "Percentage change is calculated as ((new value minus old value) divided by old value) times 100. If a price goes from $80 to $100 that is a 25% increase. If it drops from $100 to $80 that is a 20% decrease."
  - q: "What is the difference between percentage and percentage points?"
    a: "Percentage describes a proportion relative to a base. Percentage points describe the arithmetic difference between two percentages. If interest rates go from 2% to 5% that is a 3 percentage point increase but a 150% percentage change."
  - q: "How do I find what percent one number is of another?"
    a: "Divide the part by the whole then multiply by 100. For example 30 is what percent of 120? Divide 30 by 120 to get 0.25 then multiply by 100 to get 25%."
  - q: "Can I calculate reverse percentage?"
    a: "Yes. If you know the final value after a percentage increase or decrease you can work backwards. Divide the final value by 1 plus the decimal rate for an increase, or 1 minus the decimal rate for a decrease."
