<section class="how">
  <h2>How to Use This Percentage Calculator</h2>
  <p>There are three modes and you just pick whichever one matches the question you have.</p>
  <p>The first mode answers "what is X% of Y?" which is the most common question. Type the percentage and the base number and the result appears immediately, no button press needed.</p>
  <p>The second mode calculates percentage change between two values. Useful for price comparisons, exam score improvements, sales figures, anything where you want to know how much something rose or fell in percentage terms.</p>
  <p>The third mode answers "X is what percent of Y?" which is useful when you already know the part and the whole and need to express the relationship as a percentage.</p>
